// D10041 — the open twin of `map-index-store-hole-param`: the map is an un-annotated `Map()`, so
// its value type is the parameter's hole and the instance has no value slot unless the pin names it.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function fill(p) {
  const m = Map()
  m["k"] = p
  m
}
// @@VALUE@@
fill(7)
// @@TYPE@@
Map<string, i32>
// @@TEST@@
v["k"] != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v["k"] ?? 0)
// @@MISS@@
print("miss")
// @@WANT@@
7
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: a value read back out of a map is `V | null`, and this proof indexes the container itself
map_set: the same `V | null` read as `map_value`
map_value_place: the same `V | null` read as `map_value`
argument: an un-annotated parameter only READ as a map pins neither half, which the checker refuses by design (`holeMapDemandOpen`)
early_return_guard: the same read-only map parameter as `argument`
